WEBVTT

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:36.540
"This hand... Here. Put this 
human hand through the door,

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.420
and say, 'Please give me 
mittens that fit this hand.'

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:47.320
Understand? You must not offer this hand,"

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.000
the mother fox told her son.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.830
"Why not?" asked the little fox.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:02.080
"When humans realize they're 
speaking to a fox,

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.870
they won't sell you mittens.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:10.790
In fact, they'll catch you 
and put you in a cage."

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:17.780
<b>Sakura and Akiho's Lullaby</b>

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:19.880
How was that?

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.530
Ya didn't stutter at all.
 I heard everything perfectly.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.530
Sounds good!

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:24.770
Really?

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:25.750
Yep!

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.800
I can tell ya got up early 
every morning to practice.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.170
<b>Buying Mittens 
By Niimi Nankichi</b>

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.240
Since Rika-chan lent me this picture book,

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.160
I hope I can read it well.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.590
You'll be reading with Yukibunny, right?

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.380
Yeah! Yukito-san volunteers to read 
to people at lots of places.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.220
Just the two of you?

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.480
That was the plan...

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:51.680
But I'm thinking of inviting one more.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:55.650
Reading... to others?

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.420
You've never heard of it?

00:02:58.420 --> 00:02:59.640
No, I'm sorry.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.530
You take things like picture 
books, and... um...

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.620
It's like story time.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.750
Like reading stories to children,
 you might call it.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.090
Oh, I understand!

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.500
So you read books?

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.620
Yeah! I'm reading to kids at the 
pediatrics ward this time.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.740
That's amazing, Sakura-san!

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.620
It really isn't...

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.690
Hey, want to join me?

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.130
You too, Syaoran-kun!

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.390
I thought it'd be nice 
if we did it together.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.730
Then we could all act out different parts!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.040
B-But my Japanese isn't that good...

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.470
You'll be just fine.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.620
When you read "Ten Nights of 
Dreams" in Japanese class before,

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.230
it sounded lovely.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.950
I can't do it.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.570
I was awful in our elementary school plays.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.190
Your portrayal of a princess 
was very... unique,

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:51.970
but as a prince, you were wonderful!

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.460
You really were.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.020
How do you know?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.810
Anyway, I can't.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.410
The piano, then!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.260
How about you play the piano 
to accompany the story?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.220
Well, Daidouji is better at piano than me...

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.850
I have to shoot the video.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.010
His face is all red...

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:32.490
Sakura-chan's attack 
reduced his HP to zero.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.820
F-Fine! I can do just the accompaniment!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.940
Thanks!

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.450
S-Sure...

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.400
Akiho-chan?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.250
I-If I wouldn't be in your way...

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.960
Thanks!

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.850
S-Sure...

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.720
Akiho-chan's HP just dropped to zero, too.

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.240
<i>Well, now! You'll be playing 
the accompaniment?</i>

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.210
That's how it turned out, for some reason.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.220
<i>What sort of story is it?</i>

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.460
It's about a fox that goes to buy mittens.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.450
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.200
<b>Syaoran</b>

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.850
<i>Because it's cold.</i>

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:15.150
But doesn't he have his own fur?

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.620
<i>Even with fur, it's still cold in winter.</i>

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.950
Does the story have a happy ending?

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.370
<i>Yeah, I guess so...</i>

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.070
Well, then, as you requested,

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:33.390
I will email you a score appropriate to 
such a story in the next thirty minutes.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.280
I appreciate it.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:36.640
<b>Tell him to switch to a video call</b>

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.860
<i>Other than that, is everything going well?</i>

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.270
<i>You don't call me very often.</i>

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:58.170
<b>Buying Mittens 
By Niimi Nankichi</b>

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.560
Meiling filled you in, didn't she?

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.280
<i>She did.</i>

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.080
<i>She told me how much she enjoyed 
being in Japan again,</i>

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.130
<i>and how happy she was to see her friends.</i>

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:07.800
<i>She also told me that you seemed 
to have made a serious decision.</i>

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:14.520
I know that from the day you came home 
to the day you returned to Japan,

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:20.170
your mother gave you truly 
rigorous training.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:24.890
And I know that you grew much stronger.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.430
<i>But I am still worried.</i>

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:35.890
<i>After all, my only wish is to protect you, 
Syaoran-sama, no matter what happens.</i>

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.710
<b>Syaoran</b>

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:38.700
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:41.200
So please...

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.790
<i>Turn on video mode so that 
I can see your face.</i>

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.050
<i>My sisters are there, aren't they?</i>

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:48.880
Gulp!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.210
<i>I know you're there.</i>

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:51.690
Perfect timing.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:57.170
Please stop sending me pictures of food 
and large videos through messages.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:07:01.340
<i>But doesn't seeing delicious food and 
your beautiful sisters make you happy?</i>

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.440
You send too many.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.990
<i>What?!</i>

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:12.870
<b>Syaoran</b>

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:10.590
<i>Wei, I'll be watching for the piano score.</i>

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:12.530
Understood.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.010
In that case, we'll just have 
to send him a longer video.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:18.990
Agreed!

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.960
<b>Rumble</b>

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.890
You are so kind.

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.640
That is why I worry about you.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:39.080
The little fox walked beneath 
his mother's belly,

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:42.440
<b>Onomatopoeia and Phenomimes</b>

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:46.480
blinking his round eyes and looking 
all around as they went on.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:52.070
<b>Buying Mittens 
By Niimi Nankichi</b>

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.660
Eventually, their... pass?

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.060
Do you mean "their path"?

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.250
Yes, that's it.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.600
What is that?

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:04.420
I'm writing down the parts I need to 
be careful on or made mistakes with.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.280
You're not writing them in the book itself?

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.340
I can't write in this book!

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:16.930
Its author worked so hard to write it.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.680
You truly do like books, don't you?

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:22.820
It's "love"!

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.350
F-For books, I mean...

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:31.180
All this practice must 
be making you thirsty.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:36.410
<b>Onomatopoeia and Phenomimes</b>

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:35.230
<i>There was no need to correct 
that statement, Akiho.</i>

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:35.020
How about some tea?

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:36.390
Y-Yes, please.

00:08:37.290 --> 00:08:39.280
It's black tea with honey today?

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:42.780
Yes, since honey is good for the throat.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.160
Have some chocolates, too.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.030
Thank you.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.560
This seems like a lot for 
just the two of us.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:57.880
Don't worry. It'll be just enough.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.450
<i>To fill my beautiful body, that is.</i>

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.940
<b>Public Reading</b>

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.940
<b>Night on the Galactic Railroad 
Buying Mittens</b>

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.090
With so many things on his mind,

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.690
Giovanni turned away from the 
professor without a word.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.700
<b>Night on the Galactic Railroad</b>

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:20.850
Thinking that he had to hurry home 
to bring his mother the milk

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:23.810
and tell her that his 
father was coming home,

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:29.730
he ran along the river bank toward 
town as fast as he could.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:31.600
The end.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.970
Thank you.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.270
That was really good!

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:38.870
Where is "Heaven"?

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:39.720
Well...

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.730
He <i>is</i> good.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:42.740
Yes.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.970
Yukito-san was amazing!

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.660
But, but... C-Can I really do this?

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:51.240
I-I'm getting nervous, too.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:52.880
It'll be fine.

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.490
You both practiced so much.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:57.500
Yeah...

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:58.940
Right.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.950
Here. Wear these.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:25.090
A cold winter came from the north

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.890
to the forest where a mother 
fox lived with her son.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:35.120
One morning, the little fox tried 
to step outside their den,

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:36.310
I figured you'd have outfits ready.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:42.240
but with a cry of "Ah!" he tumbled back 
down to his mother, covering his eyes.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.570
They're very simple, though.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.220
But he refused to wear one.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.400
It's best that he can play 
the piano comfortably,

00:10:45.970 --> 00:10:47.960
so I gave up on him this time.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.370
This time.

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:55.500
She didn't want her sweet 
baby to develop frostbite,

00:10:55.980 --> 00:11:00.890
so she decided to go into town that night

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:04.270
and buy woolen mittens that 
would fit his little paws.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:09.580
The dark, dark night came, 
wrapping the forests and fields

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.030
in its shadows like a great blanket,

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:17.310
but no matter how it tried,
 the snow was such a bright white

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:19.660
that it shone through the shadows.

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:26.380
After some time, their path brought 
them in view of a single light.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.060
When the little fox saw it, he said,

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:37.170
"Mom, look how low that star has fallen!"

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:46.350
"That's not a star," his mother 
said as her feet froze in place.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.900
"It's the light of the town."

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.830
Seeing the town's light

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:57.190
reminded the mother fox of the time she 
and her friend had gone into town

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:00.390
and had a terrible experience.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.220
Her friend had ignored her pleas to stop

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:09.370
and tried to steal a duck from a farmhouse.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:13.900
The farmer had spotted them and 
chased them, and they fled,

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.890
barely escaping with their lives.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:24.480
With no other choice, she decided 
to send her son into town alone.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:28.500
"My son, hold out one paw..."

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:32.020
Said the mother fox.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:37.370
She held his paw in her own for a time,

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.260
and turned it into an adorable 
human child's hand.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.840
Wow!

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.590
Isn't that amazing?

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.020
"It's a human hand.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.620
Listen to me, son.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:56.660
When you go into town,
 you'll see many human homes.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:13:02.560
You must find the one that has a 
sign with a rounded hat on it.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:10.660
When you find it, knock on 
the door and say, 'Hello!'

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:16.350
When you do that, a human will open 
the door a tiny bit from the inside.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:19.220
Then, you must put this hand...

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:24.080
Here. Put this human hand through the door,

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:29.230
and say, 'Please give me 
mittens that fit this hand.'

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:30.730
Understand?

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.610
you must not offer this hand,"

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.560
the mother fox told her son.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:46.600
He saw signs with bicycles, glasses, 
and many other things on them,

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:53.890
some newly drawn with fresh paint,
 and others peeling like an old wall.

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:58.930
But he had no idea what any of them meant,

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:01.890
as he had never been to town before.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:05.950
Finally, he found the hat shop.

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:13.860
There hung the sign with 
the large, black silk hat

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:17.780
that his mother had directed him to,
 illuminated by a blue light.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:24.330
The little fox knocked on the door 
as his mother had instructed.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.270
"Hello!"

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:32.220
Then he heard the sound 
of movement inside,

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:35.390
and the door opened just a few inches,

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:41.160
making a ribbon of light stretch out 
over the white snow on the road.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:45.590
The little fox was so startled 
by the bright light

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:49.090
that he put the wrong 
hand through the door,

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:57.050
the one his mother had told him 
he mustn't let the humans see!

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:58.550
No! He can't do that!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.230
Yeah! That's bad!

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.490
He'll get chased, like the other foxes!

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:04.590
He'll get caught!

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.720
Oh, boy...

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:09.110
Wh-What should we do?

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:32.270
"Please give me mittens 
that fit this hand!"

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:37.800
The hat maker thought, "What's this, now?

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:44.200
That's a fox's paw. A fox's paw 
is asking me for mittens.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:49.930
He must be planning to 
buy them with leaves."

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:55.220
So he said, "Give me money first."

00:15:56.310 --> 00:16:00.720
The little fox obediently 
handed the hat maker

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:03.090
the two silver coins he'd been holding.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:08.760
The hat maker held each coin 
between a thumb and forefinger,

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.430
and tapped them together.

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:13.290
When he did, they made 
a fine clinking noise,

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:19.030
so he knew that they were 
real coins and not leaves.

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:23.590
So he took a pair of children's 
woolen mittens from a shelf

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:26.590
and handed them to the little fox.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:33.080
The little fox thanked the hat maker 
and turned back the way he'd come.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:40.270
"Mom said humans were scary, 
but that wasn't scary at all.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:45.260
He saw my paw, but he didn't 
do anything to me!"

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:47.100
Thought the little fox.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:52.950
Then, as he passed beneath a window, 
he heard a human's voice inside.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:57.750
It was a such a gentle, such a beautiful,

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:01.840
such a calming voice.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:10.530
Go to sleep, go to sleep,

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:16.140
here on Mama's breast.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:22.360
Go to sleep, go to sleep,

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:27.080
here in Mama's arms.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:36.670
The little fox knew without a doubt that 
the voice belonged to a human mother.

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:42.990
After all, his own mother
 sang in such a gentle voice

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.740
when she rocked him to sleep, too.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:53.140
Hearing this made him miss his mother,

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:56.880
so he went running back to 
where the mother fox waited.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:04.130
The mother fox had been trembling with worry

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:08.390
as she waited for her son to return.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:14.960
When he did, she held him to her warm 
chest and felt like weeping with joy.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:19.790
The two foxes returned to the forest.

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:25.040
The moonlight made their coats shine silver

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:29.340
and cobalt shadows stretch from their feet.

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:33.100
"Humans aren't scary at all!"

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.910
"Why do you say that?"

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:39.410
"Well, I put my real paw 
through the door by mistake.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:43.410
But the hat maker didn't try to catch me.

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:47.820
He just gave me these nice mittens."

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:53.520
And then he clapped his 
mittened paws together.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:58.030
Shocked, his mother gasped, "Oh, my!"

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.850
And then she murmured, "I wonder 
if humans really are good.

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:08.310
I wonder if humans really are good..."

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.230
The fox finished his errand!

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:18.730
The hat maker was so nice!

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.110
You're so cool!

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:21.420
Play a song from TV!

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:23.920
You're a really good singer!

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:25.350
Thank you...

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:26.550
Why do you sound so nervous?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.280
Hey, when will you come read to us again?

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.320
Well, um...

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.160
Let's practice together again.

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:36.060
Okay!

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:43.330
Ya really did a good job today.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:44.850
Thanks.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:47.700
It got a little crazy in the 
middle, but I had fun.

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.330
I think I'd like to be in the 
audience next time, though.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:54.950
If ya wanna see today's, 
Tomoyo got it on video.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.390
Release!

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:58.190
Record!

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.600
I used it before we started.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.670
When'd ya do that?

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.350
Show me what you've recorded!

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.670
It's Tomoyo-chan!

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.070
That means I'll be there, too!

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:31.870
Who's that old dude?!

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:33.770
Akiho-chan?

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:39.850
Syaoran-kun?

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.160
None of them are here...

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:50.570
This isn't... today's reading.

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:55.300
I guess I did it wrong...

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:02.450
Kero-chan?

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.220
I just got an email from Yue.

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:08.130
He said he's got a ton of 
sweets that expire today,

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:11.940
so I can have 'em. I'm headin' over there!

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:13.390
Huh? Now?

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:15.260
But it's late!

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:17.050
Expiration date!

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:22.250
I'm pretty sure you'd be fine even if 
they were a week past their date.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:25.750
How rude!

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:28.020
This is it?

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:32.520
These were in the recording Sakura 
played with the Record card.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.940
These uniforms were used 
over thirty years ago.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:41.920
They don't match the ones the 
nurses at today's reading wore.

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:43.190
Which means...

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:48.020
The card recorded footage from the past.

00:21:54.130 --> 00:21:55.080
Yeah.

00:21:55.990 --> 00:21:59.010
Sakura doesn't seem to have a clue, though.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:05.460
The only magicians I've met who were powerful
 enough to show the past are Clow and...

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:08.990
only three others.

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:14.330
She inherited the cards from 
a descendant of Clow,

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:17.590
then transformed them into her own cards.

00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:19.790
And now, she's still...

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:25.510
I knew her magic had 
gotten stronger, but this strong?

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:29.980
Sakura's magic has grown strong.

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:32.580
Immensely strong.

00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:35.840
We need to contact Eriol.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:38.260
No matter what it takes.

00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:12.150
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.600
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.600
<b>K</b>

00:24:13.210 --> 00:24:15.520
Time for another energetic 
"Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:15.520 --> 00:24:18.750
Today we're introducin' Akiho's 
stuffed bunny, Momo!

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.830
Her blue muffler adds a colorful 
touch to her white body,

00:24:20.830 --> 00:24:22.970
and she wears a fancy accessory 
on her left ear.

00:24:22.970 --> 00:24:26.120
Her bent right ear and beauty mark below 
her right eye give her character.

00:24:26.120 --> 00:24:28.440
I thought she seemed like 
a sophisticated plushie,

00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:31.660
but shock and surprise outta 
the blue... she's alive!

00:24:30.070 --> 00:24:31.070
<b>Closed     Open</b>

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:31.070 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.820
Looks like the full cast is here now! 
Can't wait to see what happens next!

00:24:34.820 --> 00:24:38.120
I'm so excited, I'm gettin' hungry!
 I want some homemade chocolates, too!

00:24:38.120 --> 00:24:39.850
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.000
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:24:41.060 --> 00:24:45.880
Syaoran-kun and I are going to visit 
my great-grandfather at his villa.

00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:47.930
What is it he wants to give me?

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:51.440
Next time, "Sakura, Rainbows, and Grandpa."

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura, Rainbows, and Grandpa</b>

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:54.620
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:24:57.930
<b>End</b>
